Q: Unhandled Exception: [firebase_auth/invalid-credential] Invalid OAuth response from apple.com A: <pre><code>
  Future&lt;void&gt; _signInWithApple() async {
    try {
      setState(() =&gt; _loading = true);

      final rawNonce = _generateNonce();
      final nonce = _sha256ofString(rawNonce);

      // 1️⃣ Apple Sign-In
      final appleCredential = await SignInWithApple.getAppleIDCredential(
        scopes: [
          AppleIDAuthorizationScopes.email,
          AppleIDAuthorizationScopes.fullName,
        ],
        nonce: nonce,
      );

      // 2️⃣ Firebase OAuth
      final oauthCredential = OAuthProvider(&quot;apple.com&quot;).credential(
        idToken: appleCredential.identityToken,
        rawNonce: rawNonce,
        accessToken: appleCredential.authorizationCode
      );

      // 3️⃣ Firebase Login
      final userCredential =
          await FirebaseAuth.instance.signInWithCredential(oauthCredential);

      final user = userCredential.user!;
      final isNewUser = userCredential.additionalUserInfo?.isNewUser ?? false;

      // 4️⃣ Handle email correctly (VERY IMPORTANT)
      String email = user.email ?? '';
      String name =
          '${appleCredential.givenName ?? ''} ${appleCredential.familyName ?? ''}'
              .trim();

      if (isNewUser) {
        await FirebaseFirestore.instance.collection('users').doc(user.uid).set({
          'uid': user.uid,
          'email': email, // real OR private relay
          'name': name,
          'provider': 'apple',
          'createdAt': FieldValue.serverTimestamp(),
        });
      }

      if (!mounted) return;

      ScaffoldMessenger.of(context).showSnackBar(
        const SnackBar(content: Text('Apple login successful')),
      );

      // TODO: Navigate to Home / Complete Profile
      // Navigator.pushReplacement(context, ...);
    } on FirebaseAuthException catch (e) {
      debugPrint('Apple Login FirebaseAuthException');
      debugPrint('code: ${e.code}');
      debugPrint('message: ${e.message}');
      rethrow;
    } catch (e) {
      debugPrint('Apple Login Unknown Error: $e');
      rethrow;
    } finally {
      if (mounted) setState(() =&gt; _loading = false);
    }
  }
</code></pre>
<p>Use this function according to your codition</p>

Q: prevent form submission when all input text fields are empty but allow submission when any of them in not empty with jquery A: <p>Yes, this is a correct and commonly used approach for basic client-side form validation.</p>
<p>By using the onsubmit attribute and returning false from the <code>validateForm()</code> function, the form submission is successfully prevented when the input field is empty. This allows you to check user input before the form is sent to the server.</p>
<p>A small improvement is to remove inline JavaScript and attach the validation logic using an event listener instead. This keeps HTML and JavaScript separated and improves code readability.</p>
<p>Example:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;form id=&quot;myForm&quot;&gt;
  &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; id=&quot;username&quot;&gt;
  &lt;input type=&quot;submit&quot; value=&quot;Submit&quot;&gt;
&lt;/form&gt;

&lt;script&gt;
document.getElementById(&quot;myForm&quot;).addEventListener(&quot;submit&quot;, function (event) {
  var name = document.getElementById(&quot;username&quot;).value;
  if (name === &quot;&quot;) {
    alert(&quot;Please enter a name&quot;);
    event.preventDefault();
  }
});
&lt;/script&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>This method is recommended as it follows better coding practices while achieving the same validation result.</p>
